<title>USA: Westinghouse ratio not set for spinoff.</title>
<headline>Westinghouse ratio not set for spinoff.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ratio for the planned spinoff of Westinghouse Electric Corp's industrial operations, to be made in a stock dividend, has not yet been set, chief financial officer Frederic Reynolds told a news conference.</p>
<p>Shareholders would receive a dividend of shares in Westinghouse Electric Co or WELCO, the new company formed from the current Westinghouse's industrial operations.  </p>
<p>Company chairman and chief executive Michael Jordan also said it has not yet been determined what the broadcasting entity will be called.</p>
<p>&quot;That's a good question. We've got a lot of dispute over that,&quot; Jordan said. &quot;This is like having a new brand of Doritos.&quot;</p>
</text>
